<title>SENEGAL: Senegal sees 60,000-tonne 1997/98 cotton output.</title>
<headline>Senegal sees 60,000-tonne 1997/98 cotton output.</headline>
<dateline>DAKAR 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senegal is expected to produce 60,000 tonnes of seed cotton in the 1997/98 (May-March) agricultural campaign against 38,000 tonnes in 1996/97, an official at the state cotton company SODEFITEX told Reuters.</p>
<p>SODEFITEX is 77.5 percent state-owned, but is earmarked for privatisation.</p>
</text>
